<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak c.bank sets 1-day repo tender at 1000 CET.</title>
<headline>Slovak c.bank sets 1-day repo tender at 1000 CET.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Slovakia, looking to add liquidity to the interbank money market, said on Wednesday it had set a tender for one-day securities repurchase agreements for 1000 CET.</p>
<p>The American-style tender would have a minimum rate of 9.7 percent, the NBS said in a statement.</p>
</text>
